      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A new series of rigid analogues (1a-g, 2a-g) of the previously reported analgesic 3-cinnamyl-8-propionyl-3,8-diazabicyclo[3.2.1]octane (I) and its reverted isomer 3-propionyl-8-cinnamyl (II) were synthesized, in which the cinnamyl substituent is incorporated in benzocondensed bicyclic systems. Binding assays for the affinity towards mu receptors indicated that, while in the reverted series 2 the beta-naphthylmethyl (2d) and the benzocycloheptenylmethyl derivative (2g) favorably compared with II, all compounds 1 displayed a mu-affinity lower than that of the parent I. Modeling studies suggest that the flexibility of the cinnamyl side chain plays an important role for activity."},
